":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald F. Clarke","x":"…to your point, of speed and security that people don't have to roll down their windows, there's cost reduction for parking, things, right, in not having 2 lanes but having one where one is automated, like you see on the toll and security in the case of fuel, where particularly females are…","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2018 Q4","e":"cpay","d":"2019-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Ronald F. Clarke","x":"The prices are higher because there's more people kind of in the game, kind of in our game, which I think is taking prices up.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2018 Q4","e":"cpay","d":"2019-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Oscar Turner","x":"And then does more of a partnership approach have implications on pricing power long term?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2020 Q2","e":"cpay","d":"2020-08-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric R. Dey","x":"I mean, certainly, over the short term, we are looking at ways to rightsize the business so we can maximize profitability over the short term.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2020 Q2","e":"cpay","d":"2020-08-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric R. Dey","x":"So I would say over the medium term, short -- in the short term, I would say, \"Hey, we're going to have some cost savings over the medium term.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2020 Q3","e":"cpay","d":"2020-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Charles Freund","x":"I'd like to note that in an effort to streamline my prepared remarks, all of my rates of change are on a year-over-year basis, unless otherwise noted.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2023 Q4","e":"cpay","d":"2024-02-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Sheriq Sumar","x":"So just wanted to get some context as to what's the pricing power over here, and can we expect the same trajectory?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q1","e":"cpay","d":"2025-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ron Clarke","x":"As it relates to tariffs, we're not a particularly sensitive tariff stock that is, we won't directly pay tariffs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q1","e":"cpay","d":"2025-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ron Clarke","x":"Our international businesses in the U.K. and Brazil operate intra-country, so not subject to tariffs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q1","e":"cpay","d":"2025-05-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ron Clarke","x":"The slightly increased full-year guide reflects the Gringo acquisition in Brazil, and that's net of the $6 million unfavorable spread shortfall we saw in Q1.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q1","e":"cpay","d":"2025-05-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Alissa Vickery","x":"Consequently, we’re maintaining our 2025 guidance, and now adding Gringo, which adds to revenue but is neutral to cash EPS.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q2","e":"cpay","d":"2025-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Peter Walker","x":"While there is little incremental clarity on US trade policy and tariffs, the global coverage and nature of our business is such that markets outside of North America are doing quite well and made up for some softness in North America.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/corpay-cpay-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q2","e":"cpay","d":"2025-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ron Clarke","x":"I think the tariff situation, uncertainty, whatever you want to call it, is landing differently on different companies, both geographically, like it's landing, you know, affected us more here in North America because of the early, you know, Canada, Mexico posture.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/corpay-cpay-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q4","e":"cpay","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald F. Clarke","x":"I guess for the follow-up, also on the cross-border business, we get some questions from time to time on a potential Supreme Court ruling on IEPA and maybe some impact that could have to CFAI even the tariffs are rolled back.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/corpay-cpay-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q4","e":"cpay","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald F. Clarke","x":"But I guess in the event that there is some level of rollback of tariffs, any idea on how that could play out across either your corporate payments business or maybe the vehicle payments business as well?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/corpay-cpay-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2025 Q4","e":"cpay","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald F. Clarke","x":"Certainly on the cost takeout side on some of the revenue synergies that are super easy, like, coming across to our contracts and things.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/corpay-cpay-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2026 Q1","e":"cpay","d":"2026-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Michael Infante","x":"And then maybe, Peter, just in terms of some of the tariff comp dynamics, you obviously had some pull forward, some uncertainty in North America.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/08/corpay-cpay-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2026 Q1","e":"cpay","d":"2026-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Peter Walker","x":"As such, we are encouraged by our strong Q1 and it strengthens our conviction on achieving our increased full year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/08/corpay-cpay-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2026 Q2","e":"cpay","d":"2026-08-05","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Peter Walker","x":"Taken together, these results reinforce our confidence in the durability of our growth model and support our decision to increase full year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/12/corpay-cpay-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CPAY 2026 Q2","e":"cpay","d":"2026-08-05","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Peter Walker","x":"We are raising our full year guidance for adjusted EPS to $27.35 per share at the midpoint growing 28% year over year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/12/corpay-cpay-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[33,1,6172,0,0,0,4422,1381],[34,1,6371,0,0,0,4795,1232],[35,1,5377,0,0,0,3855,1205],[36,1,5303,0,0,0,3636,1270],[37,1,3742,0,0,0,2437,1026],[38,1,4053,0,0,0,2641,1088],[39,1,4805,0,0,0,3379,1088],[40,1,5245,0,0,0,3606,1324],[41,1,4799,0,0,0,3127,1326],[42,1,3931,0,0,0,2634,991],[43,1,4285,0,0,0,2441,1443],[44,1,4065,0,0,0,2474,1310],[45,1,4108,0,0,0,2366,1410],[46,1,4956,0,0,0,2949,1607],[47,1,4081,0,0,0,2665,1079],[48,1,4889,0,0,0,3219,1241],[49,1,4110,0,0,0,2472,1189],[51,1,5185,0,0,0,2724,2051],[52,1,4842,0,0,0,3191,1279],[53,1,4121,0,0,0,2478,1341],[54,1,5743,0,0,0,3735,1635],[55,1,5409,0,0,0,3242,1772],[56,1,3733,0,0,0,2184,1224],[57,1,10118,0,0,0,8088,1713],[59,1,6716,0,0,0,4903,1452],[60,1,9935,0,0,0,7509,2017],[61,1,8582,0,0,0,6380,1752],[62,1,10625,0,0,0,8239,1965],[64,1,9597,0,0,0,7401,1572],[65,1,6032,0,0,0,5018,823],[66,1,8755,0,0,0,1595,6432],[67,1,9101,0,0,0,7107,1648]],"cinema":[[33,1,